<%# Inline notice inside a page - not a flash, which the layout owns.

    design.md's alert shape: a tint, a matching border, and matching ink, so the panel reads as a
    message rather than as a card. Same rounded-2xl as the cards it sits among, so a page of them
    lines up on one corner radius.

    It was hand-rolled twice, on portfolios#show and stocks#index, with an inline SVG, a
    `border-l-4` bar and yellow-700/800 ink. Two copies of a notice is how the two pages ended up
    saying the same thing at different sizes.

    Measured on their own tints: amber-900 on amber-50 is 8.75:1, amber-800 6.84:1,
    blue-900 9.52:1, blue-800 8.01:1, and the amber-700 icon 4.84:1.

    Locals:
      title - the headline, required
      body  - optional supporting line
      tone  - :warning (default) or :info
      icon   - optional lucide name, defaults per tone
      testid - optional data-testid

    An optional trailing control (a dismiss) can be passed as a block; render with `layout:`. %>
<% tone = local_assigns.fetch(:tone, :warning).to_sym %>
<% tones = {
     warning: { surface: "border-amber-200 bg-amber-50", title: "text-amber-900",
                body: "text-amber-800", icon: "text-amber-700", glyph: "triangle-alert" },
     info: { surface: "border-blue-200 bg-blue-50", title: "text-blue-900",
             body: "text-blue-800", icon: "text-blue-700", glyph: "info" }
   } %>
<% t = tones.fetch(tone, tones[:warning]) %>

<%# A bare tone-coloured glyph, never an icon tile. design.md: the tile pattern is for contexts
    where the icon is the subject - a KPI card, a section header - and it assumes a white surface.
    A banner is text with a marker beside it, which is what Polaris Banner, Material, Carbon,
    Primer flash and Atlassian SectionMessage all ship. %>
<%# tag.div, so an absent testid is omitted entirely: interpolating an optional attribute yields
    an *unquoted* one, which CSS and Capybara selectors will not match. %>
<%= tag.div class: "rounded-2xl border #{t[:surface]} p-4 #{local_assigns[:class]}",
            role: "status",
            data: { testid: local_assigns[:testid] } do %>
  <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
    <%= lucide_icon local_assigns.fetch(:icon, t[:glyph]), class: "mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 #{t[:icon]}" %>
    <div class="flex-1">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium <%= t[:title] %>"><%= title %></p>
      <% if local_assigns[:body].present? %>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm <%= t[:body] %>"><%= body %></p>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <%# An optional trailing control - a dismiss, usually. Passed as a block, so a caller that has
        one does not have to rebuild the whole panel to get it. %>
    <% if block_given? && (action = capture { yield }).present? %>
      <div class="shrink-0"><%= action %></div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
